    {
      "title": "A short glossary",
      "summary": "The few words that come up on almost every slide.",
      "body": [
        "Each term is explained fully the first time it matters. Come back to this list if a word on a later slide feels unfamiliar.",
        "Two ideas matter more than any single definition:",
        {
          "ul": [
            "<b>Everything is numbers.</b> Text becomes whole numbers, those become vectors, and the model just does maths on the vectors.",
            "<b>Behaviour comes from learned numbers.</b> Nobody writes an LLM's knowledge or style by hand. <mark>Billions of numbers are adjusted during training until the model predicts text well, and everything it can do comes from those numbers.</mark>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "note": "A handy comparison with software: <b>training</b> is like a very long, very expensive build that produces a file (the weights). <b>Inference</b> is running that file. Most of this course is about inference; the <i>Training</i> chapter covers the build.",
          "kind": "dev"
        }
      ],
